  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="kalaqtor-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">כלקטור</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">klqṭwr</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">kalaqṭor</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="kalaqtor-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>feature (of the face)</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>χαρακτήρ</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>שהיה סבור שהוא אברהם, שהיה כלקטור פניו דומה לו</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">Vat 1: 95,8</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">III 1233: 9</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>He thought it was Abraham, since the feature of his [Jacob’s] face was similar to him.</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">60,7 [II 647: 5]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">קלסטר</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 109 [31d: 54]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">קלסתר</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Correct form should be <term xml:lang="jpa">כלקטר</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">klqṭr</term>. Usual form is <term xml:lang="jpa">כלקטורין</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">klqṭwryn</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">kalaqṭorin</term> (see <bibl type="modern">AC IV 291a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 291b</bibl>, <bibl type="modern">Levy II 342b-343a</bibl>). Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">καρακτήριον</term> (<bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 291b</bibl>). GenR location mentioned by <bibl type="modern">Shoval-Dudain 96a</bibl> (she does not distinguish between the different forms). See <ref type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa">קלסטר</ref>.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>ΜΥ ΙΙΙ</title>
                  <citedRange>1233</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
